fighting between government forces and  the m23 rebel group has sent thousands  of people on the run in eastern  democratic republic of congo it's not  the first time  we were just told that m23 have come  back again they emerged from the forest  to attack the congolese government at  the moment we are just seeing government  forces driving up and down the road but  we don't have a solution yet  nine years ago m23's fighters took  control of swathes of territory along  the border with neighbouring rwanda  it's widely believed to be a proxy of  rwanda's government although rwanda  denies it  congo's army blames rwanda for the  recent attacks which started on tuesday  congolese officers paraded these two  prisoners in front of journalists in the  city of gomer and said they were rwandan  soldiers fighting for the armed group  the m23 supported by the rwanda defence  forces has carried out incursions and  attacks on jrc military positions in  chanzu and rignoni in rochiro territory  m23's fighters have taken control of  some villages near the border with  uganda  the group denies having foreign support  the m23 rebellion is a congolese  movement and doesn't benefit support  from any neighboring country the  accusations of the drc is to just cover  their incapacity on the ground as for  the current ongoing fighting we are  defending ourselves against the  different attacks that we have been  facing from the government army since  many days  thousands of people have crossed the  border into uganda to get away from the  fighting uganda and rwanda have both  been accused of meddling in eastern  congo and displacing people ever since  they invaded in the 1990s  congo has one of the world's largest un  peacekeeping missions  it's rarely effective at stopping  violence but in 2014 it helped defeat  m23 with a strengthened mandate and  extra troops sent from tanzania malawi  in south africa  the defeat was a high point for congo's  army too his soldiers flushed out the  rebel group with international support  now it's short of resources and  struggling to control parts of the east  people here waiting to see how far m23  will go this time and if the congolese  army can stop them  malcolm webb al jazeera
 

